@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# Matching Paper stance diagnostic
+
+Measure how the saved Paper policy produces stance and commanded translation,
+using the same controls as WR2's completed stance diagnostic. Use the frozen
+`paper-walking-baseline` source at `a4f693d` and its native Brax submodule
+`1414780`. The module checks the saved source, model/reference hashes and actual
+training package versions before execution.
+
+## Run on the GPU
+
+Use an isolated checkout for this diagnostic while the main TB folder remains
+available for development. After applying the diagnostic patch, run from
+`~/projects/toddlerbot/.worktrees/paper-stance-diagnostic`:
+
+```bash
+git submodule update --init --recursive
+export UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT="$HOME/projects/toddlerbot/.venv-paper-blackwell" UV_PYTHON=3.10
+export PYTHONPATH="$PWD/toddlerbot/brax"
+uv run --no-sync -m toddlerbot.locomotion.diagnose_stance \
+  --run-dir ../../results/toddlerbot_walk_ppo_20261015_194347 \
+  --output ../../results/toddlerbot_walk_ppo_20261015_194347/stance_diagnostic \
+  --seeds 22102
+```
+
+This reuses the environment that completed Paper training: Python 3.10,
+JAX/JAXlib 0.6.2, MuJoCo/MJX 3.2.4 and native Brax 0.10.5. `PYTHONPATH` selects
+the diagnostic checkout's pinned Brax source even when the shared environment
+has an editable installation pointing at the original TB folder. If the
+environment needs installation, follow the Blackwell section of
+[PAPER_WALKING.md](PAPER_WALKING.md) in this checkout. The diagnostic requires
+a GPU by default.
+
+The default checkpoint is the native exported policy at `200089600/policy`.
+The saved run folder must also contain `env_config.json`, `train_config.json`,
+`provenance.json` and its archived `locomotion/` source. Native inference uses
+Swish, the saved network widths, deterministic NormalTanh actions and identity
+observation preprocessing, matching the completed Paper trainer.
+
+Use `--checkpoint ../../results/toddlerbot_walk_ppo_20261015_194347/180080640/policy`
+and a separate output directory to inspect the retained 180M survival reference.
+A completed output directory cannot be overwritten.
+
+## Paired controls
+
+| Control | Actions sent to the native controller |
+| --- | --- |
+| `learned` | Deterministic saved-policy actions |
+| `hip_roll_reference` | Replace left/right hip-roll coordinates with bounded reference actions |
+| `leg_reference` | Replace all 12 leg coordinates with bounded reference actions |
+
+For each intervened coordinate, convert the current reference motor angle with
+`clip((q_ref - q_home) / 0.25, -1, 1)`. The fixed-home action mapping, one-tick
+delay, physical joint limits, nominal motor controller and collision simulation
+then apply normally. Report reference angles outside the action range rather
+than expanding that range. The learned actor receives each control's changing
+observations, so its remaining outputs can respond to the intervention.
+
+Each control runs forward/backward .10, forward/backward .05, left/right .05
+and standing, using identical reset keys for each seed. Commands are held for
+1,000 control ticks at 20 ms, or 20 TB-equivalent seconds. WR2 uses its recorded
+size and clock normalization: 824 ticks at 20 ms, approximately the same
+TB-equivalent duration. TB measurements have normalization scale 1.0.
+
+The diagnostic disables domain randomization, physical pushes and white
+observation noise. Native reset still samples yaw and action-origin bias when
+those flags are false. For this nominal comparison, reset is rebuilt from the
+native grounded reference pose at zero yaw and the action-origin bias is zero.
+TB's deterministic torque-dependent backlash observation offset remains active
+at the saved scale .02. The run report records these overrides explicitly.
+
+These controls measure action execution and coordination. A reference control
+can fall or move poorly without establishing the quality of a trained policy.
+Use the existing randomized XY suite for the full walking benchmark.
+
+## Outputs and comparison
+
+The output contains `summary.json` and 21 compressed raw `.npz` traces, one per
+control/command/seed. Additional seeds each add another 21 traces. The report
+includes checkpoint and configuration hashes, verified source, package versions,
+backend/devices, control clock, mass/gravity and the nominal reset overrides.
+
+- **Tracking and movement:** torso-frame XY velocity mean/std, mean per-tick
+  vector command error, root displacement in the initial commanded heading
+  frame and net velocity. With zero initial yaw, that heading frame equals the
+  world frame. Compare commanded-axis progress and cross-direction drift.
+- **Joint execution:** actor request, amended current request, delayed request,
+  delivered position target, actual angle, current reference, clipping and
+  reference reach for each leg motor. A separate reconstruction must match the
+  target actually passed to the native controller. `pipeline.ctrl` is torque.
+- **Support:** native floor-contact classification at the saved 1 N threshold;
+  single/double/no support; exact phase matching and double-support matching
+  conditional on valid ticks requesting double support.
+- **Geometry and force:** signed gap and active penetrating-contact force for
+  both ankle-roll and ankle-pitch left/right pairs; sole clearance, floor force,
+  lateral foot-body distance, native spacing reward and unweighted air-time
+  landing credit. Self-contact requires force magnitude greater than .1 N.
+
+Raw geometry and force use the cached final physics-substep frames. Forwarding
+the integrated end-of-tick qpos again can select a different instant. For offline
+gap calculation, MuJoCo 3.2.4's legacy box routine returns half penetration depth;
+native CCD measures the full depth. A legacy zero-distance check handles native
+CCD's exact-touch degeneracy. These distance queries use an offline model copy;
+the original MJX simulation and collision solver remain at the saved settings.
+
+A finite terminal tick is included once; following padding is excluded. A
+nonfinite tick is excluded and marked separately. Double-support matching is
+null when no valid tick requests double support. Retain each episode's duration
+when comparing unequal-length controls.
+
+First compare the learned TB/WR2 traces. Then use the paired reference controls
+to identify whether clearance, loaded joint tracking, support timing or drift
+changes explain the difference. Normalize WR2 distances, speeds and clocks with
+the factors recorded by its diagnostic. Report raw clearance for each robot as
+well as size-normalized clearance. Select a training correction after this
+comparison, retaining the shared Paper objectives unless the measurements
+support a specific change.
+
+## Development verification
+
+Run the focused measurement tests with the selected environment:
+
+```bash
+uv run --no-sync python -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_stance_diagnostic.py -v
+```
+
+`--steps 100 --allow-cpu` provides a short execution check in a fresh output
+directory. It exercises approximately 2.8 native gait cycles; the full GPU
+diagnostic remains the comparison artifact.
+
+## References
+
+- [ToddlerBot paper, Tables VI/VII](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.00893v2).
+- Frozen [native environment](toddlerbot/locomotion/mjx_env.py),
+  [walking rewards](toddlerbot/locomotion/walk_env.py),
+  [ZMP reference](toddlerbot/reference/walk_zmp_ref.py) and
+  [motor controller](toddlerbot/sim/mujoco_control.py).
+- [MuJoCo 3.2.4 collision detection](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/3.2.4/computation/index.html#collision-detection)
+  and [geometry-distance API](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/3.2.4/APIreference/APIfunctions.html#mj-geomdistance).
